# Both lists are asked for numbers in front of the loop. The second read took NaN for a hole because the first stood beside it as a number or nothing; the first had only Link's word on the second,
# and where Link has none (lists out of JSON.parse, parameters of a function that escapes) it stayed `undefined|number`: its hole was asked in every turn and the product asked for NaN again,
# 4 of the 17 instructions a turn. `undefined * x` and `NaN * x` are one answer for every x: the rule says where the form pays, not where it is right.
# f1 = dot
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: as-written
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: number @Double = GetArrayElement {{*}}[keyIsIntegral, isInBounds, readsHoleAsNaN, admitsInt32Storage]
# CHECK-NEXT: number @Double = GetArrayElement {{*}}[keyIsIntegral, readsHoleAsNaN, admitsInt32Storage]
